KW  - Healthcare Automation
AB  - Artificial Intelligence (AI)-powered e-triage systems are transforming patient intake and clinical decision-making by automating workflows and improving diagnostic precision. These systems address critical challenges in emergency and outpatient settings, where rapid assessment and prioritization are crucial for delivering optimal care. This paper introduces an integrated architecture comprising four core components: a Data Ingestion Module that consolidates patient information from electronic health records (EHRs), wearable devices, and intake forms; an AI Triage Engine employing machine learning algorithms to evaluate patient urgency and predict risk; a Documentation Generator utilizing natural language processing (NLP) for automated admission reporting; and a Prescription Assistant that recommends evidence-based treatments aligned with clinical guidelines. Real-world deployments in hospitals across the UAE and GCC have demonstrated substantial operational improvements, including a 45 % reduction in documentation time and an 82 % increase in patient prioritization accuracy. These advancements not only enhance patient outcomes through early detection of critical conditions but also alleviate clinician workload, reducing burnout and cognitive strain. Key performance indicators (KPIs) such as diagnostic accuracy, patient throughput, and prescription error rates validate the system's effectiveness and scalability. Despite these benefits, challenges remain in ensuring data privacy compliance, mitigating algorithmic bias, and achieving seamless integration with existing EHR platforms. Future directions include incorporating real-time analytics, expanding wearable device interoperability, enabling multilingual support, and adopting human-in-the-loop models to maintain ethical and clinical robustness. By addressing these barriers, AI-powered e-triage systems can become a cornerstone of modern healthcare, delivering adaptive, efficient, and patient-centric care at scale.
