AB  - Lack of medical and human resources often leads to major issues in emergency triage, involving patients being prioritized incorrectly and the ED being cram-full. This research paper proposes implementing an AI-driven “Medico Assistant” to revolutionize the use of triage in EDs. The ongoing triage systems use static assessments, which may cause ineffective resource allocation and delayed actions. Our novel approach integrates the usage of real-time multi-modal data, including ambient sensor data, unstructured clinical notes, Electronic Health Records (EHR), and patient-reported symptoms, using a refined deep learning architecture. Furthermore, XAI will be used to furnish coherent explanations of its findings and personalized, frugal suggestions. By enhancing ET accuracy and efficacy, it enables early critical interventions and fast-track resource usage. This “Medico Assistant” gives way to improved patient outcomes in stretched clinical environments.
