AB  - Deep learning is reshaping healthcare across medical imaging, clinical text, time-series physiology, and genomics. This review synthesizes methods and applications with emphasis on model families (CNN/UNet/ViT; RNN/Transformers), datasets and evaluation practices (AUROC/AUPRC, Dice, calibration, external validation). We summarize benefits—earlier detection, consistent triage and personalized decision support—alongside persistent challenges including data quality and shift, fairness, interpretability, privacy and regulatory alignment. To support responsible translation, we propose a practical evaluation checklist covering robustness, calibration, subgroup performance and workflow integration. We conclude with near-term research priorities: self-supervised and federated learning for data efficiency and privacy, multimodal modeling for holistic patient state and prospective validation with post-deployment monitoring. This synthesis aims to guide researchers and practitioners toward clinically credible, trustworthy AI systems.
