AB  - An understanding of animal behavior is critical for not only animal welfare reasons but for purposes of risk factor prevention, as well as human interaction. However, in trying to make sense out of their behavior, actions, emotions, and intentions, specialized knowledge is required in most instances, hence leaving most pet owners in the dark concerning what particular behavior means. It is proposed: Explainable AI Chatbot for Animal Behavioral and Medical Triage. It integrates a multimodal behavior-understanding pipeline that combines vision-based action recognition with pose estimation and contextaware reasoning models for inference of the underlying causes driving such behaviors as aggression, fear, restlessness, abnormal posture, social signaling, or environmental responses. To foster trust and usability, the system embeds an explainability module able to generate human-readable reasoning that explains “why the animal performed this action” by highlighting visual cues, movement patterns, or contextual features relevant to the prediction. And in the case of unusual, distressing, or pathological behavior, a structured medical triage dialogue is started, with specific questions to decide if veterinary attention could be required. It uses light veterinary knowledge models for screening purposes and also conveys the level of uncertainty while not offering any diagnoses that fall outside the realm of the chat bot. It offers insight on how explainable multimodal AI can close the communication divide between human beings and animals through scientific behavioral interpretation. Based on the work performed within this paper, the research on explainable animalcentric AIs has just begun.
