AB  - Long waiting times for dermatology consultations significantly impact patient satisfaction and treatment outcomes, particularly for severe conditions requiring urgent care. This work presents SkinAI: Virtual Dermatology Assistant for Triage Acceleration, an AI-driven system leveraging computer vision and deep learning to analyze images of skin conditions uploaded by patients. The system determines the urgency level of each case and prioritizes severe conditions for immediate attention, thereby optimizing resource allocation in dermatology clinics. Continuous training on diverse and updated datasets enables SkinAI to identify a wide range of skin diseases accurately, accommodating variations in skin tones and conditions. By providing rapid and precise preliminary assessments, the system empowers dermatologists to focus on critical cases, reduces waiting times, and enhances overall healthcare efficiency. Initial evaluations demonstrate high diagnostic accuracy and sensitivity for urgent cases, underscoring the potential of SkinAI to improve patient outcomes and transform dermatological practice
