AB  - This study explores the integration of Artificial Intelligence (AI) and the Internet of Things (IoT) in optometry for enhanced vision screening and diagnosis. Using IoT-enabled smart devices and AI models, including a convolutional neural network (CNN), the system achieved a 95.6% accuracy in classifying retinal diseases. SHAP analysis provided interpretability, with refractive error emerging as the most influential feature in visual acuity classification. Real-time monitoring enabled continuous assessment of visual parameters, triggering automated alerts for early intervention. Clinical validation showed high sensitivity (93.2%) and specificity (91.7%), while a user satisfaction score of 4.5 out of 5 indicated patient acceptance. The AI-IoT integrated system offers a scalable solution for proactive eye care, facilitating early diagnosis and personalized management. Future research will focus on integrating advanced diagnostics and expanding tele-optometry services to improve accessibility and effectiveness in diverse healthcare settings.
