AB  - We present a multi-cloud, serverless deployment framework and a complementary AI pipeline for outbreak management in large healthcare networks. The framework extends an operational rules-based system deployed during COVID-19 (15,000 employees across 295 facilities) by adding portable Infrastructure-as-Code (IaC), cost-aware scaling, and healthcare-grade security. The AI pipeline integrates facility-level forecasting (LSTM), individual risk scoring (XGBoost), anomaly detection (Isolation Forest), and contact-network analytics, with explainable AI (XAI: SHAP, LIME, counterfactuals) embedded directly into clinician workflows. Evaluation on anonymized operational logs and calibrated synthetic multi-disease streams shows improvements over (i) a rules-only production baseline and (ii) a single-vendor “siloed AI” deployment: higher predictive accuracy, lower end-to-end latency, $\sim 30 \%$ lower cost per million events, and increased clinician agreement. We explicitly delineate (A) benefits from multi-cloud portability (e.g., disaster recovery, data residency, cost control) and (B) benefits from AI augmentation. Together, these yield a portable, explainable, and cost-conscious foundation for outbreak management beyond COVID-19.
