AB  - MRI shows detailed brain structure without invasive procedures, yet gliomas, meningiomas, and pituitary adenomas can appear similar on T1-weighted axial scans. We develop a single-modality classifier that couples a ResNet branch, which extracts local textures and edges, with a Vision Transformer that models longer-range relations across the slice. To aid review, Grad-CAM heatmaps accompany each prediction, highlighting the regions that most influenced the decision and making failure cases easier to inspect. Evaluated on the Figshare benchmark, the system attains precision of $0.9812,0.8239$, and 0.9679 for meningioma, glioma, and pituitary classes, with F1-scores of $0.9474,0.8733$, and 0.9705, respectively. These results indicate that combining convolutional and transformer pathways yields accurate classification while preserving interpretability. The approach is compact, single-sequence, and compatible with routine clinical workflows, offering an explainable assistant for triage and second-read scenarios without additional contrast or sequences. Prospective validation and external datasets will be explored in future work.
