AB  - Proper prediction of disease based on symptomatic presentation is a major issue in medical diagnosis especially in situations where resources are limited such as in contexts where advanced diagnostic facilities are not readily available. This research will suggest a new hybrid deep learning framework, which is a combination networks to predict multiple diseases on the basis of multi-symptom patient data. The suggested model of hybrid CNN-BiLSTM got a high accuracy of 99.39% with precision of 99.46, recall of 99.39 and F1-score of 99.40. K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN) recorded the highest accuracy of 99.49 percent but the proposed model performed better than the conventional ones such as Support Vector Machines (93.29 percent), logistic regression (92.28 percent), and Naive Bayes (85.37 percent). The ensemble top five algorithm did 99.39% accuracy. The deep learning hybrid technique using attention mechanism has a strong contribution to the prediction accuracy in diseases and retains the interpretability in terms of attention weights. The high performance of the model in a wide range of disease classes evidences its viability in the real-life medical application especially in the cases of initial screening and triage.
