AB  - We present ASIST-TBI, a Vision Transformer deep neural network model to forecast neurosurgical intervention from non-contrast head CT in acute TBI patients. It receives CT input in the form of a programmatic pipeline of voxel resampling, preprocessing, and 3D patch spatial embedding before being classified by a transformer encoder. It was trained on 2806 prior cases and validated on a held-out set of 612 subsequent cases, and ASIST-TBI performed well with 87.6% accuracy, 0.91 AUC, 88.2% sensitivity, and 86.8% specificity. On external data set, the model performed at 84.3% accuracy and AUC of 0.89. Our approach was more predictive in ability and practicable in the clinic than baseline method, aided with visualization-based interpretability with Grad-CAM. ASIST-TBI is a useful addition to computer-based triage assistance with a suitable and robust solution for enhancing decision-making for acute emergency management in neurotrauma.
