AB  - Pneumonia remains a serious respiratory infection for which early identification can improve clinical outcomes. Yet, reading chest radiographs is time-consuming and can vary across observers, especially where experienced radiologists are scarce. This work introduces an automated pneumonia screening model that merges a ResNet-50 convolutional feature extractor (for local patterns) with a Swin Transformer component (for global context reasoning). We evaluate the approach on the Kaggle Chest X-ray Pneumonia dataset using 5,216 training images and 624 test images, obtaining 83.65 % accuracy and 92.05 % recall, which indicates strong sensitivity for triage-oriented use. For interpretability and practical deployment, Grad-CAM heatmaps are generated and a lightweight web interface is provided. Key implementation choices and hyperparameters are documented to support reproducibility and further development.
