AB  - Highly crucial to find diabetic retinopathy (DR) early on in clinical settings where resources are limited, so that visual loss does not become permanent, especially when the disease is found. EffDR-Net is a deep learning framework that is based on the EfficientNet-B3 architecture. The goal of this study is to equip EffDR-Net with the ability to assess the severity of DR using high-resolution fundus photos automatically. EffDR-Net uses compound-scaled convolutional neural networks (CNNs) and was trained and tested on the Kaggle EyePACS dataset. Kaggle made EffDR-Net. This dataset contains a large number of retinal photos; however, they are not evenly distributed across the five distinct severity levels of diabetic retinopathy (DR). Computer networks (CNNs) are utilized to enhance the accuracy of models and streamline computer tasks. To address common issues such as overfitting, the system employs transfer learning, aggressive data augmentation, dropout regularization, and batch normalization, among other techniques. There are also dropout regularization and batch normalization. The model struggles to accurately identify moderate to severe stages of DR, as the class distributions are not evenly distributed, and the features distinguishing between classes are not clear. Most of the time, these limits are caused by factors other than the ones mentioned. Overall, the model can be very accurate and converge quickly, although it does have some problems with appropriately identifying these stages. A lot of testing using class-wise accuracy, recall, F1-scores, and Grad-CAM visualizations shows that EffDR-Net is quite effective at identifying early DR. Still, it requires further refinement to classify advanced phases reliably. The results of the exhaustive evaluation lead to this conclusion. The information collected during the evaluation supports this conclusion. This study makes a significant contribution to the development of artificial intelligence-based ophthalmic screening skills by demonstrating how EfficientNet can be utilized to categorize patients in a real-world emergency room setting, along with its advantages and disadvantages.
