AB  - Manual interpretation of OCT images requires extensive expertise and is time-consuming, limiting clinical accessibility. This paper presents a novel automated approach for OCT retinal disease classification using Vision Transformer (ViT) enhanced with Convolutional Block Attention Module (CBAM). Our method leverages transformer self-attention to capture long range dependencies while incorporating spatial and channel attention for improved feature representation. We evaluate our approach on the OCT2017 dataset with 84,484 images across four categories: CNV, DME, Drusen, and Normal retina. The proposed ViT-CBAM model achieves superior performance with 97.8% accuracy, outperforming state-of-the-art CNN and baseline transformer models. Ablation studies demonstrate CBAM integration provides 2.3% accuracy improvement. The model exhibits excellent computational efficiency, making it suitable for real-time clinical deployment. Beyond accuracy improvements, the proposed pipeline maintains reproducibility with clearly defined preprocessing, stratified validation split, and open benchmark protocols, and offers strong interpretability through attention map analysis, which highlights clinically meaningful regions and may facilitate decision support and triage in high-volume ophthalmic screening in real-world workflows and resource-constrained settings globally.
